Request bodies
JSON rows use application/json. Send real runtime values and omit unused optional keys. Dates are YYYY-MM-DD, timestamps are ISO 8601 with a timezone, and IDs described as UUIDs are backend IDs. For multipart send a real file with a filename, let the transport generate the boundary, and serialize scalar form values as text. Common auth is described above.
Body profile	Required fields	Optional fields and rules
Enrollment	image_base64 string	allow_re_enroll boolean, default false. JSON only. The server resolves the current employee.
Face punch, V1 JSON	image_base64 string	location object with numeric latitude, longitude and optional accuracy in metres, plus top-level notes, device_info, work_mode strings. Work modes are office, remote and field. Check-in can reject missing GPS. Client IP comes from the request connection.
Face punch, V1 multipart	file binary	Flat form fields latitude, longitude, accuracy, notes, device_info, work_mode. Provide the latitude and longitude together. V1 check-in reads an optional Idempotency-Key header. Verified replay is a separate V2 contract.
Break capture	JSON image_base64 string or multipart file binary	JSON supports location with latitude, longitude, optional accuracy, plus notes and device_info. Multipart supports top-level latitude, longitude, accuracy, notes and device_info. Start and end both require a capture. The multipart break parser accepts jpg/jpeg/png/webp and a maximum file size of 10 MiB.
Geofence	Top-level latitude number, longitude number	accuracy number in metres. Read data.inside_geofence, data.status and data.message.
Mobile punch, V2 PWA	Top-level image_base64 nonempty string, latitude number −90…90, longitude number −180…180 and header Idempotency-Key string 8–128 chars	accuracy number ≥0, notes string ≤500, device_info string ≤255, client_captured_at timestamp. JSON only. Retrying with a changed payload and the old key can produce 409. A fresh capture is a new request.
Core check-in	JSON object. The schema declares all keys optional. Tenant policy can require image_base64.	Top-level image_base64, latitude, longitude, ip_address, device_info, notes. Use only when the existing product deliberately supports the core policy-driven workflow.
Core check-out	JSON object. All keys are optional.	Top-level latitude, longitude, ip_address, device_info, notes. The canonical face checkout has its own required image.
Manual edit	audit_reason string	check_in_time timestamp, check_out_time timestamp, status string. Submit a meaningful reason and actual changed values.
Correction	request_date date, reason string	attendance_id UUID, requested_check_in timestamp, requested_check_out timestamp. Display the returned status.
Shift change	requested_shift_id UUID, start_date date, reason string 1–1000 chars	end_date date ≥ start date. Uses the schema declared in the mounted me.py.
Create shift	name nonblank string 1–50 chars, start_time and end_time as distinct time strings	Send 24-hour HH:MM. An end earlier than start means overnight. The handler generates code and reads these three fields.
Edit shift	JSON object with the desired changes	name, start_time, end_time with the same formats. PUT and PATCH delegate to the same edit behavior.
Create roster	employee_id UUID, shift_date date	shift_id UUID, shift_type string, start_time and end_time time strings, notes string. Upsert. For a working shift supply both custom times together or omit both. A selected shift can supply the times.
Bulk roster	Nonempty employee_ids UUID array, and either nonempty dates date array or start_date plus end_date dates, inclusive	Same optional shift fields as create roster. The service caps employee count × date count at 2,000.
Edit roster	JSON object with the desired changes	shift_date, shift_id, shift_type, start_time, end_time, notes. PUT and PATCH share a handler. Roster types in this snapshot are DAY, NIGHT, MORNING, EVENING, OVERTIME, ROTATION, HOLIDAY, OFF, WEEKLY_OFF, LEAVE, TRAINING and WFH.
Monitor analysis	startDate, endDate as ISO date strings with these exact camel-case keys	department string. Validate date order before submission.
Settings	JSON object	config key/value object, default empty. This handler persists recognized keys such as working_days, office_timing, timezone and currency. Verify read-after-write before offering other policy or geofence controls.
AI shift plan	company_id UUID from authorized tenant context, period_start and period_end dates, employee_ids UUID array	department string, plan_type string (WEEKLY by default, also MONTHLY, ROTATION, HOLIDAY), constraints string and model string. This is a separate planning workflow.
Unlock	reason string ≥2 chars and the payroll cycle UUID in the URL	The lock action takes no body. Verify the mounted version in the payroll workflow.


